#activity-title(centered: true)[Conducting Summer Camp for Rural Students to Enhance Digital Skills and Awareness]

#v(4mm)
#set par(justify: true)

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.1 Overview]

#h(36pt)This activity was conducted as part of a summer camp organized by Akanksha Charitable Trust, Puttur, in collaboration with Vivekananda College of Engineering and Technology (VCET), Puttur, and Tata Consultancy Services (TCS). The programme was conducted from 02-05-2024 to 21-05-2024 with the objective of providing rural students with basic digital knowledge, improving their technical skills, and creating awareness about future educational and career opportunities.

#h(36pt)During the programme, 30 rural students were trained in various digital and productivity-oriented skills. The sessions focused on introducing students to HTML, CSS, Canva, Office Tools, G-Suite, and Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The concepts were explained through practical demonstrations and interactive activities so that the students could easily understand and apply the skills.

#h(36pt)The students were introduced to the basics of web development using HTML and CSS, which helped them understand how simple web pages are created and designed. They were also trained in Canva for creating posters, presentations, and other creative digital content. Basic Office Tools and G-Suite applications were demonstrated to improve their productivity and familiarity with commonly used digital platforms.

#h(36pt)As part of the programme, students were also guided and encouraged to participate in a hackathon. They were introduced to basic problem-solving, idea development, teamwork, and presentation skills required for a hackathon. This provided them with an opportunity to apply their newly acquired knowledge to practical problems.

#h(36pt)The programme also created awareness about the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and their importance in addressing social, economic, and environmental challenges. Interactive discussions and practical activities helped students gain confidence and develop interest in technology and learning.

#h(36pt)Overall, the summer camp successfully contributed to improving the digital literacy, creativity, communication, problem-solving ability, and confidence of rural students. The activity also encouraged students to explore technology as a tool for education and future career development.

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.2 Use of Technology]

- Training students in HTML and CSS for basic web page development.
- Demonstration of Canva for designing posters, presentations, and creative content.
- Use of Microsoft Office tools for preparing documents and presentations.
- Introduction to G-Suite/Google Workspace and its productivity applications.
- Use of digital presentations and practical demonstrations to make learning interactive.
- Guidance on using technology for hackathon idea development and presentation.
- Use of online and digital learning resources to encourage independent learning.

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.3 Sustainable Development Best Practices]

- Promoting Quality Education (SDG 4) by providing digital and technical education to rural students.
- Reducing the digital knowledge gap by improving access to basic technology skills.
- Encouraging students to use technology for education, creativity, and problem-solving.
- Creating awareness about the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
- Developing communication, teamwork, creativity, and confidence among students.
- Encouraging rural students to explore higher education and technology-oriented career opportunities.
- Promoting responsible and productive use of digital tools.

#text(weight: "bold", size: 16pt)[2.4 Outcome of the Activity]

#h(36pt)The summer camp provided 30 rural students with practical exposure to essential digital and productivity tools. Students gained basic knowledge of web development, digital designing, office applications, and online collaboration tools. The hackathon guidance further helped them improve their problem-solving, teamwork, creativity, and presentation skills. The programme successfully enhanced their digital awareness and encouraged them to consider technology and higher education as pathways for their future development.

